  "description": "Here is how to read the MiniMax M3 config.json. The architecture class is MiniMaxM3SparseForCausalLM, which is the transformers (or equivalent) module that wires embeddings, attention, the MLP, and the language-modelling head that turns hidden states into next-token logits.\n\nhidden_size is 6,144: that is the width of every residual stream vector. The embedding matrix is therefore 200,064 \u00d7 6,144: each token id owns a vector of that width.\n\nnum_attention_heads is 64, so each head sees 128 dimensions (6,144 / 64). The ratio test is hidden_size / num_attention_heads = 6144 / 64 = 128. 128 is a multiple of 32 (NVIDIA warp-friendly), and a multiple of 16 (Huawei cube-friendly), and a power of two (Triton / FlashAttention-friendly). From this number alone you cannot name the training chip.\n\nnum_key_value_heads is 4, so this is grouped-query attention (GQA): 64 query heads share 4 key/value groups, so the KV cache is about 16\u00d7 smaller than full MHA.\n\nnum_hidden_layers is 60: the stack is that many transformer blocks deep.\n\nintermediate_size is 3,072. In a SwiGLU MLP this is the high-dimensional workspace: the 6,144-wide stream is projected up, activated with swigluoai, then projected back. Labs usually round this width to a multiple of 128 or 256 so it tiles on the chip.\n\nmax_position_embeddings is 1,048,576 tokens \u2014 the context window in the config. There is no rope_scaling entry, so the rotary positions are used as-is. rope_theta is 5000000: that is the wavelength of the rotary embedding. A larger theta keeps distant tokens from aliasing after a full rotation.\n\nvocab_size is 200,064. 200,064 is divisible by 128. bos/eos ids, when present, are just two special rows in that table; the padded vocab is often larger than the tokenizer\u2019s real inventory.\n\ntie_word_embeddings is false, so the input embedding matrix and the output LM head are separate learned matrices rather than a shared transpose.\n\ntorch_dtype is bfloat16. Brain floating point keeps FP32\u2019s exponent range with less mantissa, which avoids the overflow/underflow of a tiny exponent at the cost of noisier decimals \u2014 and it halves the on-chip footprint versus FP32. NVIDIA A100s were the first NVIDIA chips with native BF16; Huawei Ascend 910-class parts also prefer BF16/FP16 on the cube.\n\nThe copy of config.json is from https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3/blob/main/config.json."
